.TH SCRIPTURES 1
.SH NAME
scriptures \- the scriptures, offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scriptures
.RI [ place ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scriptures
reads the scriptures from churchofjesuschrist.org offline: footnotes,
full-text search, highlights, notes and tags, several chapters open at once
in tabs, and notes synced with a Church Account (Gospel Library). It is the
.B Scriptures
app of the desktop
.RB ( /etc/apps/scriptures.app ),
a window of the desktop's own kind.
.PP
The first start shows an empty library:
.B Download...
picks the language and the volumes; the standard works are about 1,600
pages and take a few minutes. The tabs open last time come back at the
next start. Each
.I place
(a path that starts with
.BR / ,
as the content uses:
.BR /scriptures/ot/gen/1 )
is opened as well.
.SS Keys
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
search
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
every note, in a tab
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
show or hide the library
.TP
.BR Ctrl+5 " .. " Ctrl+9
tab 5 .. 9 (Ctrl+1 .. 4 are the desktop's workspaces)
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
the previous and next chapter
.TP
.BR Ctrl+C ", " Ctrl+V
copy the selection with its reference; paste in a field
.TP
.B middle button
open a chapter, a result, a note or a link in a new tab
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.scriptures/
the library: chapters, the search index,
.BR notes.json ,
.BR settings.txt ,
the session
.TP
.B ~/.scriptures/account
the Church Account's session (mode 600)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR atlas (4),
.BR app (5)
.SH BUGS
The desktop sends no Alt and no Ctrl with a click, and keeps Ctrl+T and
Ctrl+Tab: use the tab bar instead.
